    "result_text": "All 268 tests pass with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires the owner response to include a `displayName` field formatted as `LastName, FirstName`. The `Cp06Tests` acceptance test creates an owner then reads the field back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so it needed to be part of the shared `OwnerDto`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. OpenAPI codegen regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field, getter/setter, and Jackson binding.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")` on `toOwnerDto`, so the derived name is computed whenever an owner is mapped to its DTO (covers both the create response and the GET response, since both go through the mapper).\n\nNo new OfficeFloor function or YAML was needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/`RespondWithOwner` steps already map through `OwnerMapper`, so the computed field flows through automatically.",
